add('john_rematch','MeteorFalls_1F_2R_Text_JohnPostRematch','John recalls daily Pokemon battles throughout fifty years together.',
'''soft_smile~Their ordinary Tuesday apparently included a scheduled rivalry.|A repeated activity can become part of how a partnership remembers time.|Long habit. Glad they still enjoy it together.|I wonder which little pre-battle routine never changed.|Some memories grow from what you do together every day.|An epic relationship made partly from thousands of familiar little scenes.|A domestic schedule with an unusually lively competitive section.|Repeated practice must have given them very detailed knowledge of each other.|A ritual can keep changing while remaining recognizably theirs.|The shared history is what makes the habit feel special.|I'd love to hear about the day they unexpectedly did something different.''')
add('john_register','MeteorFalls_1F_2R_Text_JohnRegister','John politely invites us to battle the couple again if paths allow.',
'''soft_smile~A future visit to a very well-established double act.|Another match could let us observe how their coordination develops.|Gladly, when we're nearby and the team is ready.|It's kind that he leaves the timing open.|A familiar welcome makes returning to a difficult place nicer.|A courteous invitation from a cast I'd happily revisit.|A social appointment with an unusually impressive combined history.|We could compare the strategies without rushing through the conversation.|A meeting can leave a small thread between very different journeys.|Good manners give the challenge a warm shape.|I'd enjoy seeing what they remember about us when we return.''')
add('nicolas','MeteorFalls_1F_2R_Text_NicolasPostBattle','Nicolas wonders when the long harsh road to being best will end.',
'''neutral~Best is a destination that keeps moving its furniture.|A broad ranking is less actionable than a specific improvement goal.|Aim for better first. Best can wait.|The whole road can feel heavier when you only look at its far end.|A break doesn't cancel the progress already made.|An endless superlative can make every chapter feel unfinished.|An ambition with extremely unhelpful opening hours.|One measurable skill would make the next practice less vague.|A far wish needn't consume the small ground beneath today's feet.|A strong personal style matters more than chasing every comparison.|I'd ask what would make the next day feel worthwhile even without the title.''')
add('nicolas_rematch','MeteorFalls_1F_2R_Text_NicolasPostRematch','Nicolas uses our continued strength as motivation for his own growth.',
'''soft_smile~Our practice has become somebody else's renewable homework.|A consistently challenging opponent can provide useful comparison.|We'll keep working. He can meet us stronger.|It's nice when a rival finds encouragement in the gap.|His team still deserves time to recover between tests.|Two recurring characters have agreed not to let the story stand still.|A rather demanding form of mutual encouragement.|He could track which part of the gap actually narrows.|A familiar challenge can give effort a clear direction.|A good rivalry leaves room for both people to develop their own strengths.|I'd like to see a new idea from him, not just more of the old one.''')
add('nicolas_register','MeteorFalls_1F_2R_Text_NicolasRegister','Nicolas wants contact so he can understand our strength.',
'''soft_smile~A contact request with a very competitive research question.|He can learn more by discussing decisions than only repeating battles.|We can compare notes. No secret miracle required.|It's flattering that he thinks there's something worth understanding.|A quiet conversation might help as much as another hard match.|A curious rival is more interesting than an unquestioning admirer.|A study of our power may include disappointingly ordinary practice.|We could explain one interaction rather than hand him a whole plan.|An honest question can turn a comparison into a connection.|He wants to look beneath the result, which is a better starting point.|I'd be curious which moment he most wants explained.''')
add('meteor_archie','MeteorFalls_1F_1R_Text_ArchieFarewell','Archie warns us to watch Magma before departing.',
'''neutral~A warning is useful even when the messenger has his own agenda.|We can take the caution without accepting every part of his account.|We'll watch both groups. Decide by what they do.|The farewell feels more serious after that confrontation.|The people caught between them matter more than the rivalry.|A self-appointed guide has left us with a partial map of the conflict.|A useful warning wearing a suspiciously one-sided jacket.|Observe the actions directly instead of borrowing his entire conclusion.|A path can be watched without walking behind whoever pointed at it.|His confidence shouldn't decide whose story we believe.|I'd remember the warning and keep noticing what doesn't fit it.''')
add('cozmo','MeteorFalls_1F_1R_Text_MeetProfCozmo','Cozmo explains being tricked into guiding Magma, who stole his meteorite.',
'''neutral~He thought he was helping a visit, not supplying a theft.|He was misled about the purpose of the expedition.|Not his fault they lied. Focus on what they took.|He sounds shaken and embarrassed at the same time.|Someone should let him explain without making him feel foolish.|A trusted guide has been used as a supporting character in someone else's scheme.|An honest mistake made worse by dishonest guests.|His observations could help reconstruct what happened and where they went.|Being deceived should not erase his right to be heard.|They abused his knowledge, which is different from him choosing their plan.|I'd listen to the details he remembers once he has time to steady himself.''')
add('cozmo_revisit','MeteorFalls_1F_1R_Text_WhatsTeamMagmaDoingAtMtChimney','Cozmo worries what Magma will do with the meteorite at Mt. Chimney.',
'''neutral~That is a much bigger worry than a missing rock.|Their destination and the stolen object give the concern a concrete basis.|Worth checking. No need to guess the worst as fact.|He sounds stuck on the part he can't explain.|The people near the mountain may need help too.|An unanswered question is pointing beyond the scene of the theft.|A rock-related mystery has become alarmingly volcanic.|We should verify the setup there instead of inventing a mechanism.|A stolen thing can carry a shadow farther than its owner knows.|His worry deserves an answer grounded in what actually happens.|I'd keep his question in mind when we see what they've built.''')
add('seafloor_promotion','SeafloorCavern_Room1_Text_Grunt1PostBattle','An Aqua grunt wants promotion so he can order others around.',
'''annoyed~A management plan consisting entirely of becoming someone else's nuisance.|That ambition centers control rather than the responsibility of leading.|Power's not a reward for wanting to boss people.|He sounds more interested in authority than the people involved.|A leader should make work better for the people doing it.|A supporting character has mistaken cruelty for career development.|An exceptionally clear warning about the next supervisor.|He could learn to solve a problem before asking to assign it to someone else.|A higher place doesn't make an unkind wish wiser.|A better title won't improve the attitude wearing it.|I'd notice how he treats people who can't offer him a promotion.''')
add('seafloor_cramped','SeafloorCavern_Room1_Text_Grunt2PostBattle','A grunt complains the stolen submarine is cramped.',
'''smug~The stolen ride has declined to provide luxury seating.|A vehicle designed for specific use may not suit an improvised crowded trip.|Then maybe don't steal people's transport.|He sounds as if the journey was less glamorous than promised.|The discomfort doesn't excuse taking it from its owners.|The grand escape has received an unfavorable passenger review.|A criminal adventure with poor legroom. How terribly inconvenient.|Capacity should have been considered before their ambitious loading plan.|Taking a thing doesn't mean understanding the life it was built for.|An expensive entrance can still be an uncomfortable one.|I'd remember the ordinary complaint behind their dramatic operation.''')
add('seafloor_question','SeafloorCavern_Room3_Text_Grunt5PostBattle','A grunt admires our defiance while admitting they cannot question the boss.',
'''neutral~The alarming part is how normal not asking has become.|An organization that forbids scrutiny makes its own errors harder to correct.|He can question him too. Shouldn't need our permission.|He sounds almost surprised that saying no is possible.|Being afraid to ask is a problem worth noticing.|A minor antagonist has glimpsed an alternative to following the script.|The first unsettling thought: perhaps obedience was never compulsory.|He should examine the purpose before judging our right to challenge it.|A question can open where a command has kept a person small.|He noticed our independence. I hope he keeps some for himself.|I'd watch whether the admiration becomes a question he asks aloud.''')
add('seafloor_shelly','SeafloorCavern_Room3_Text_ShellyPostBattle','Shelly regrets we are not Aqua members able to enjoy the boss\'s promised world.',
'''neutral~The fabulous world seems short on invitations to disagree.|A promised benefit doesn't establish that the method is justified.|We'll keep our judgment. She can keep the uniform.|It's strange being welcomed and threatened by the same cause.|A better world should care about the people already living in it.|A recruitment speech has skipped the chapter about who bears the cost.|A utopia with suspiciously strict membership conditions.|We need evidence about consequences, not admiration of our utility.|A future that cannot hear refusal may not be gentle.|Her compliment doesn't make the offer less troubling.|I'd judge the promise by what they're doing here, not how grandly she describes it.''')
add('seafloor_lost','SeafloorCavern_Room4_Text_Grunt3PostBattle','A grunt cannot find the exit and insists he is not frightened.',
'''neutral~The exit is missing whether or not his pride is frightened.|We can address the navigation without debating his emotional state.|Needs a way out. No shame in saying it.|I wouldn't make him prove how calm he feels.|A clear direction is more useful than teasing.|A stranded antagonist is allowed a practical problem without a dramatic confession.|I also prefer my fear to remain off the official report.|Establish the last known point before trying another passage.|A lost person can need help without first naming the feeling.|Let him keep his composure while we discuss the route.|I'd ask which turns he remembers, not whether he's scared.''')
add('seafloor_map','SeafloorCavern_Room4_Text_Grunt4PostBattle','A grunt blames his partner for leaving the map aboard the submarine.',
'''neutral~The map has stayed with the vehicle instead of the people needing it.|A shared navigation plan shouldn't depend on one easily forgotten item.|Blame won't draw a route. Work together.|It's harder to think when someone's making the mistake personal.|They need a way back more than an argument.|The missing prop is inconvenient; the hostile dialogue isn't helping.|A team has discovered that insults are poor substitutes for cartography.|Reconstruct the known route before adding more uncertain turns.|A shared mistake can be met with shared patience.|Calling a partner useless won't make the partnership work better.|I'd listen for which of them still remembers something helpful.''')
add('zigzagoon','MtPyre_1F_Text_RestingPlaceOfZigzagoon','A mourner remembers a cherished Zigzagoon at its resting place.',
'''sad~I'd stay quiet enough to let them tell us about Zigzagoon if they want.|A remembered habit might be easier to share than the whole loss.|Give them room. Be there if they want company.|I wonder which little thing they miss most on an ordinary day.|That affection deserves a gentle listener, not a hurried answer.|A beloved life has more to its story than this final place.|A name can leave a much larger silence than anyone expects.|There's no problem here that needs a clever solution from us.|What was cherished can remain close in a small familiar memory.|They shouldn't have to make the grief look tidy for visitors.|I'd remember the name and listen without turning away from the quiet.''')
